1
00:02:16,608 --> 00:02:18,008
Looks like a burial .

2
00:02:18,033 --> 00:02:19,742
In the road ?

3
00:02:25,516 --> 00:02:27,711
Driver , what is it ?

4
00:02:27,735 --> 00:02:30,671
It 's a funeral , Mademoiselle .

5
00:02:30,696 --> 00:02:33,640
They are afraid of the men who steal dead bodies .

6
00:02:34,251 --> 00:02:38,183
So they dig the grave in the middle of the road

7
00:02:38,207 --> 00:02:41,608
where people pass all the time .

8
00:02:50,608 --> 00:02:56,592
Well , that 's a cheerful introduction for you to our West Indies .

9
00:03:29,839 --> 00:03:33,259
Do you know where is the house of monsieur Beaumont ?

10
00:03:57,697 --> 00:04:00,400
Zombies ! Aller vite ! Allez !

11
00:04:07,774 --> 00:04:10,189
It felt like hands touching me !

12
00:05:00,615 --> 00:05:03,381
Why did you drive like that , you fool ? We might have been killed !

13
00:05:03,406 --> 00:05:07,538
Worse than that , Monsieur . We might have been caught .

14
00:05:07,718 --> 00:05:10,563
Caught ? By whom ? Those men you spoke to ?

15
00:05:10,614 --> 00:05:15,397
They are not men Monsieur , they are dead bodies .

16
00:05:15,849 --> 00:05:16,849
Dead ?

17
00:05:17,125 --> 00:05:20,672
Yes , Monsieur . Zombies .

18
00:05:20,696 --> 00:05:22,794
The living dead .

19
00:05:22,818 --> 00:05:29,317
Corpses taken from their graves who are made to work in sugar mills

20
00:05:29,342 --> 00:05:31,256
and fields at nights .

21
00:05:35,245 --> 00:05:38,680
Look ! Here they come !

22
00:05:47,510 --> 00:05:49,665
Look ! Look !

23
00:06:01,287 --> 00:06:04,520
Excuse me please , have you got a match ?

24
00:06:06,419 --> 00:06:12,079
Did I frighten you ? Ha , I 'm sorry . I 'm oddly enough I suppose .

25
00:06:12,104 --> 00:06:13,361
No , it wasn 't you .

26
00:06:13,386 --> 00:06:15,408
Something happened back on the road there .

27
00:06:15,616 --> 00:06:17,619
We stopped to speak to some men .

28
00:06:18,944 --> 00:06:22,813
Our driver told us that they weren 't men at all . He said they were corpses .

29
00:06:25,518 --> 00:06:26,855
Corpses ?

30
00:06:27,627 --> 00:06:29,902
Surely you don 't believe it , do you ?

31
00:06:29,927 --> 00:06:37,031
No . But I don 't know , Haiti is full of nonsense and superstition .

32
00:06:37,232 --> 00:06:41,432
They 're always mixed up with a lot of mysteries that will turn your hair grey .

33
00:06:42,033 --> 00:06:46,434
I 've been a missionary here for , oh , thirty years ,

34
00:06:46,459 --> 00:06:48,960
and at times I don 't know what to think .

35
00:06:49,437 --> 00:06:51,209
Come , let 's go in the house .

36
00:06:51,234 --> 00:06:52,849
Oh , yes , come , dear .

37
00:07:01,626 --> 00:07:04,418
Is Mr. Beaumont in ?

38
00:07:04,443 --> 00:07:06,413
You are expected , Dr. Bruner .

39
00:07:06,438 --> 00:07:10,617
Yes ... I 've been sent for to marry someone .

40
00:07:12,344 --> 00:07:14,132
Maybe you ...

41
00:07:25,902 --> 00:07:30,591
How long is it that you 've known Mr. Beaumont ?

42
00:07:30,616 --> 00:07:31,820
Oh , only a few days .

43
00:07:31,845 --> 00:07:34,774
Madeline introduced him on the docks in Port-au-Prince .

44
00:07:34,798 --> 00:07:36,329
Ah , and you ?

45
00:07:36,354 --> 00:07:38,915
I met him on the ship coming from New York .

46
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:40,905
He was very kind during the voyage .

47
00:07:41,263 --> 00:07:43,902
Madeline and I planned to be married the moment she arrived ,

48
00:07:44,056 --> 00:07:46,905
but Mr. Beaumont persuaded us to come here .

49
00:07:46,953 --> 00:07:49,686
And he promised to take me out of the bank at Port-au-Prince

50
00:07:49,711 --> 00:07:51,942
and send me to New York as his agent .

51
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:54,943
Strange .

52
00:07:56,311 --> 00:07:57,984
Very strange .

53
00:07:58,391 --> 00:07:59,391
You ...

54
00:08:01,617 --> 00:08:04,447
I 'll tell Mr. Beaumont you are here .

55
00:08:13,702 --> 00:08:15,898
It 's all right , isn 't it , doctor ?

56
00:08:15,922 --> 00:08:18,410
Oh , I guess so .

57
00:08:18,435 --> 00:08:22,705
You see I , I 've only met Mr. Beaumont once or twice .

58
00:08:22,729 --> 00:08:26,964
But he never struck me like the man who would take the trouble

59
00:08:26,988 --> 00:08:30,312
to play fairy godfather to a young couple like you ...

60
00:08:31,709 --> 00:08:32,909
Unless ...

61
00:08:34,530 --> 00:08:36,025
Unless what , sir ?

62
00:08:50,294 --> 00:08:54,126
I suppose you 'll think I 'm a meddling old fool , but ...

63
00:08:54,150 --> 00:08:56,983
You know , I 'd feel a good deal better if you 'd clear out of this place

64
00:08:57,007 --> 00:08:58,293
after you 're married ,

65
00:08:58,317 --> 00:09:00,768
and have nothing more to do with Mr. Beaumont .

66
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:08,204
The young people have arrived sir , and Dr. Bruner .

67
00:09:08,228 --> 00:09:10,487
They are waiting in the reception hall .

68
00:09:11,272 --> 00:09:14,696
Show them to their rooms , and tell them I 'm out .

69
00:09:14,916 --> 00:09:16,402
No wait .

70
00:09:17,166 --> 00:09:18,990
Perhaps I 'd better see them .

71
00:09:19,091 --> 00:09:20,902
It might look odd if I didn 't .

72
00:09:20,926 --> 00:09:22,827
Very odd , sir .

73
00:09:22,852 --> 00:09:29,247
Especially as Dr. Bruner is a trifle skeptical as to your ... motives , sir .

74
00:09:29,271 --> 00:09:31,536
Nevermind my motives .

75
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:34,331
Has that other person sent word yet ?

76
00:09:34,355 --> 00:09:35,488
No , sir . Not yet .

77
00:09:39,599 --> 00:09:40,999
He 's twenty-four hours late .

78
00:09:42,916 --> 00:09:46,603
I wish you 'd keep away from that man , sir .

79
00:09:46,903 --> 00:09:48,903
He 'll make trouble for you .

80
00:09:49,005 --> 00:09:50,630
You needn 't worry about that .

81
00:09:50,654 --> 00:09:51,975
I 'm not affraid of him .

82
00:09:51,999 --> 00:09:56,028
I 'm not easily frightened , sir . You should know that .

83
00:09:56,052 --> 00:09:58,762
But what you are planning is dangerous .

84
00:09:58,786 --> 00:10:01,321
Don 't you suppose I know that , Silver ?

85
00:10:01,345 --> 00:10:04,789
You don 't seem to realize what this girl means to me .

86
00:10:04,813 --> 00:10:07,978
Why , I 'd sacrifice anything I have in the world for her .

87
00:10:09,529 --> 00:10:12,013
Nothing matters if I can 't have her .

88
00:10:19,669 --> 00:10:23,618
I think , ah , I think you 'll like Haiti . Most people that ...

89
00:10:25,801 --> 00:10:31,521
Madeline ! I 'm delighted to see you ! Neil , you 're more than welcome .

90
00:10:31,546 --> 00:10:32,621
Thank you , sir .

91
00:10:33,348 --> 00:10:35,422
Doctor , it is very kind of you to come .

92
00:10:35,524 --> 00:10:36,925
I know what a busy man you are .

93
00:10:36,949 --> 00:10:40,185
No , ah , not at all . There is a native family live out here

94
00:10:40,209 --> 00:10:42,021
that I 've been trying to see for a long time .

95
00:10:42,562 --> 00:10:45,726
After this young couple are safely married , I 'll leave .

96
00:10:45,778 --> 00:10:48,229
But surely you will stay for dinner after the ceremony ?

97
00:10:48,334 --> 00:10:50,105
No , no , no . No , I must run along .

98
00:10:50,279 --> 00:10:54,431
That 's a great pity . We have something very special prepared for this occasion .

99
00:10:55,406 --> 00:10:58,830
It was very good of you , Madeline , to humour the whim of a lonely man .

100
00:10:58,854 --> 00:11:00,944
There was so little time to prepare ,

101
00:11:00,968 --> 00:11:03,516
I couldn 't do half the things I wanted for you .

102
00:11:04,135 --> 00:11:06,782
You 've done more than enough already Mr. Beaumont ,

103
00:11:06,807 --> 00:11:09,673
for a comparative ... giving Neil a position in The States .

104
00:11:10,121 --> 00:11:10,646
Neil ?

105
00:11:10,738 --> 00:11:12,210
Yes . Yes indeed .

106
00:11:12,234 --> 00:11:15,312
Oh , yes of course ! I 'm sure Neil will make a very good agent .

107
00:11:15,699 --> 00:11:17,640
But you must be tired after your drive .

108
00:11:17,744 --> 00:11:20,489
You get some rest . Silver !

109
00:11:22,311 --> 00:11:24,109
Silver will show you to your rooms .

110
00:11:24,593 --> 00:11:25,593
This way please .

111
00:14:52,284 --> 00:14:56,048
Delighted to see you again , monsieur Beaumont !

112
00:15:09,471 --> 00:15:11,477
Please .

113
00:15:14,574 --> 00:15:15,946
Please .

114
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:24,294
I 'm sorry to have kept you waiting , monsieur .

115
00:15:27,658 --> 00:15:29,557
I 've been on a journey

116
00:15:29,704 --> 00:15:32,283
seeking men for my mills .

117
00:15:32,992 --> 00:15:34,468
Men ?

118
00:15:34,804 --> 00:15:40,709
They work faithfully ... They are not worried about long hours .

119
00:15:42,371 --> 00:15:47,884
You ... can make good use of men like mine on your plantations .

120
00:15:47,909 --> 00:15:48,960
No .

121
00:15:50,339 --> 00:15:52,713
That 's not what I want .

122
00:15:54,908 --> 00:15:57,388
Then perhaps we should talk about the young lady

123
00:15:57,413 --> 00:15:59,449
who came to your house this evening ?

124
00:15:59,474 --> 00:16:02,439
You 've seen her ? When ?

125
00:16:03,433 --> 00:16:05,574
The road , tonight .

126
00:16:17,620 --> 00:16:21,726
There was a young man with her .

127
00:16:22,024 --> 00:16:24,426
They are to be married , tonight .

128
00:16:24,441 --> 00:16:26,577
You waited too long to do anything .

129
00:16:27,228 --> 00:16:28,807
What do you want me to do ?

130
00:16:29,010 --> 00:16:32,623
If she were to disappear , for a month ...

131
00:16:33,807 --> 00:16:37,933
What do you hope to gain by her disappearance ?

132
00:16:38,033 --> 00:16:39,232
Everything ...

133
00:16:39,543 --> 00:16:40,543
Everything ?

134
00:16:40,685 --> 00:16:43,592
Do you think she will forget her lover in a month ?

135
00:16:43,606 --> 00:16:47,562
Just give me a month . One little month .

136
00:16:48,740 --> 00:16:53,239
Not in a month . Not even a year , monsieur .

137
00:16:55,383 --> 00:17:03,383
I looked into her eyes . She is deep in love . But not with you .

138
00:17:06,123 --> 00:17:08,162
They are to be married within an hour !

139
00:17:08,405 --> 00:17:10,042
There must be a way !

140
00:17:21,045 --> 00:17:25,053
There is way .

141
00:17:27,754 --> 00:17:29,324
The cost ...

142
00:17:30,825 --> 00:17:32,325
The cost is heavy !

143
00:17:33,664 --> 00:17:38,151
You give me what I want , and you may ask anything .

144
00:18:02,055 --> 00:18:05,602
No ! Not that !

145
00:18:29,136 --> 00:18:32,881
Only a pin point , monsieur Beaumont ,

146
00:18:32,901 --> 00:18:37,632
in a glass of wine or perhaps a flower .

147
00:18:40,580 --> 00:18:44,117
Take it . The time is very brief .

148
00:18:44,285 --> 00:18:47,375
You must do your share if I am to help you .

149
00:18:50,249 --> 00:18:52,455
Keep it , monsieur .

150
00:18:56,122 --> 00:19:01,643
Keep it . You may change your mind .

151
00:19:15,451 --> 00:19:18,963
Send me word when you use it .

152
00:19:33,706 --> 00:19:38,158
- I 'll find another way . - There is no other way .

153
00:19:54,950 --> 00:19:58,292
They are driving away evil spirits !

154
00:19:58,317 --> 00:20:00,754
Close it , close it !

155
00:20:04,319 --> 00:20:05,823
Mademoiselle !

156
00:20:24,128 --> 00:20:27,469
I love you , Madeline , more than anything else in this whole world , dear .

157
00:20:27,493 --> 00:20:30,596
Heaven or hell lies in this little moment for me .

158
00:20:30,621 --> 00:20:34,923
You could raise me up to paradise or you could blast my world into nothingness .

159
00:20:34,982 --> 00:20:38,333
I can make you the envy of every woman .

160
00:20:38,834 --> 00:20:41,203
I 'd give my life to make you happy !

161
00:20:43,658 --> 00:20:45,823
Oh , listen to me dear before it 's too late !

162
00:20:46,313 --> 00:20:48,146
Don 't , please .

163
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:50,184
Don 't go into that room .

164
00:20:50,259 --> 00:20:52,639
We can be in Port-au-Prince in half an hour .

165
00:20:52,939 --> 00:20:54,840
There 's a boat sailing at midnight .

166
00:20:56,065 --> 00:20:58,318
You 've been so wonderful .

167
00:20:58,343 --> 00:21:00,746
Don 't spoil everything now .

168
00:21:04,623 --> 00:21:07,345
One last gift before I lose you forever !

169
00:21:51,535 --> 00:21:55,166
We are gathered together here in the sight of God ,

170
00:21:55,265 --> 00:21:57,367
and in the face of this company ,

171
00:21:57,766 --> 00:22:00,667
to join together this man , this woman

172
00:22:00,868 --> 00:22:02,668
in holy matrimony .

173
00:23:36,417 --> 00:23:38,208
This is the night of nights !

174
00:23:41,409 --> 00:23:45,093
A toast to the bride ! To beauty 's queen !

175
00:23:47,497 --> 00:23:49,663
Gladly , My Lord !

176
00:23:54,191 --> 00:23:57,473
Leave but a kiss within the glass .

177
00:23:59,095 --> 00:24:02,618
Fair gypsy , read my fortune .

178
00:24:09,922 --> 00:24:12,173
What do you see in the glass ?

179
00:24:13,264 --> 00:24:18,149
I see happiness ...

180
00:24:19,115 --> 00:24:25,370
I see love , far more than you can bear .

181
00:24:25,394 --> 00:24:27,500
Is that all ?

182
00:24:27,525 --> 00:24:28,891
No .

183
00:24:28,915 --> 00:24:30,684
I see ...

184
00:24:37,940 --> 00:24:39,731
I see ...

185
00:24:39,755 --> 00:24:40,755
What is it ?

186
00:24:42,287 --> 00:24:44,324
I see death .

187
00:24:46,587 --> 00:24:47,587
Madelin !

188
00:24:51,886 --> 00:24:53,224
Madeline , what 's wrong ?

189
00:24:53,965 --> 00:24:55,464
Madeline my dear , please .

190
00:25:04,788 --> 00:25:06,851
Oh , no ...

191
00:25:10,427 --> 00:25:13,448
Madeline ? Madeline ?

192
00:25:14,985 --> 00:25:16,798
Can 't we do something ?

193
00:25:16,823 --> 00:25:18,951
Please , please .

194
00:25:19,540 --> 00:25:20,879
Madeline !

195
00:25:31,420 --> 00:25:34,613
Not my wife . My wife !

196
00:26:04,593 --> 00:26:09,070
Praise of our lord and saviour and the love of god

197
00:26:09,095 --> 00:26:11,991
and the fellowship of his angels .

198
00:26:12,323 --> 00:26:15,974
Be with us ever more . Amen .

199
00:27:00,524 --> 00:27:03,808
Neil , Neil ...

200
00:27:36,008 --> 00:27:37,008
Neil ...

201
00:27:38,009 --> 00:27:39,009
Neil ...

202
00:27:40,781 --> 00:27:43,425
Neil ... Neil ...

203
00:28:37,534 --> 00:28:38,534
Look !

204
00:28:50,639 --> 00:28:51,740
Zombies !

205
00:28:53,626 --> 00:28:56,541
Yes . They are my servants .

206
00:28:57,042 --> 00:28:59,343
Did you think we could do it alone ?

207
00:29:00,608 --> 00:29:03,048
In their lifetime they were my enemies .

208
00:29:05,240 --> 00:29:11,041
Ledot , the witch doctor . Once my master .

209
00:29:11,153 --> 00:29:14,419
Secrets I tortured out of him .

210
00:29:14,443 --> 00:29:17,554
Von Gelder , the swine . Swollen with riches .

211
00:29:18,054 --> 00:29:24,754
He fought against my spells until the last . In him I have a struggling type .

212
00:29:26,415 --> 00:29:30,900
His Excellence , Richard . Once minister of the interior .

213
00:29:32,165 --> 00:29:40,165
Scarpia , Brigand Chief . Marcquis , Captain of Gendarmerie ... .

214
00:29:41,061 --> 00:29:48,482
And this , this is Chauvin , the high executioner ,

215
00:29:48,507 --> 00:29:51,568
who almost executed me !

216
00:29:55,750 --> 00:29:58,342
I took them

217
00:29:58,367 --> 00:30:03,870
just as we will take this one .

218
00:30:03,928 --> 00:30:06,371
But what if they regain their souls ?

219
00:30:08,399 --> 00:30:10,974
They would tear me to pieces .

220
00:30:11,688 --> 00:30:16,952
But that , my friend , shall never be .

221
00:31:31,188 --> 00:31:32,526
Madeline !

222
00:31:36,284 --> 00:31:38,109
Madeline !

223
00:31:43,555 --> 00:31:44,978
Madeline !

224
00:31:45,156 --> 00:31:46,616
Madeline !

225
00:33:11,907 --> 00:33:14,986
There 's two explanations that strike me ,

226
00:33:15,010 --> 00:33:18,212
either the body was stolen by the members of a death cult

227
00:33:18,236 --> 00:33:22,977
that use human bones in their ceremonies , or else ...

228
00:33:23,153 --> 00:33:24,454
Or else what ?

229
00:33:24,553 --> 00:33:26,154
She 's not dead .

230
00:33:30,460 --> 00:33:32,026
Not dead ?

231
00:33:32,876 --> 00:33:34,248
Are you mad ?

232
00:33:34,273 --> 00:33:37,525
I saw her die , the doctor signed the certificate .

233
00:33:37,549 --> 00:33:38,831
I saw them bury her .

234
00:33:39,146 --> 00:33:42,662
Now , wait a minute , wait a minute , I 'm not mad .

235
00:33:43,462 --> 00:33:46,718
But I 've lived in these islands for a good many years ,

236
00:33:46,742 --> 00:33:51,938
and I 've seen things with my eyes that made me think I was crazy .

237
00:33:53,025 --> 00:33:57,867
There are superstitions in Haiti that the natives brought here from Africa .

238
00:33:57,981 --> 00:34:03,584
Some of them can be traced back as far as ancient Egypt ,

239
00:34:03,608 --> 00:34:07,742
and beyond that yet , in the countries that was old when Egypt was young .

240
00:34:08,041 --> 00:34:10,267
Yes , but what has that to do with Madeline ?

241
00:34:10,291 --> 00:34:12,570
I kissed her as she lay there in the coffin .

242
00:34:13,860 --> 00:34:15,978
And her lips were cold .

243
00:34:17,976 --> 00:34:21,418
Let me explain . Now , just a minute , I 'll explain .

244
00:34:21,937 --> 00:34:26,722
Wherever there is a superstition , you will find there is also a practice .

245
00:34:26,746 --> 00:34:28,528
Now , do you remember what your driver told you

246
00:34:28,552 --> 00:34:30,393
the night that he took you to Beaumont 's house ?

247
00:34:30,616 --> 00:34:32,982
Oh , about those horrible creatures we saw ?

248
00:34:33,382 --> 00:34:36,102
He said they were corpses ! Taken from their graves .

249
00:34:36,126 --> 00:34:39,745
Yes - that 's the superstition ! Now for the practice .

250
00:34:40,167 --> 00:34:43,544
The ghouls that steal the dead corpses from their graves ,

251
00:34:43,569 --> 00:34:46,538
are supposed to put them there in the first place .

252
00:34:47,605 --> 00:34:49,997
Do you mean that Madeline was murdered

253
00:34:50,021 --> 00:34:52,174
so that somebody could steal her dead body ?

254
00:34:52,198 --> 00:34:53,376
Aagh ! Nonsense !

255
00:34:53,400 --> 00:34:56,195
No , no . Not her ...

256
00:34:56,220 --> 00:34:59,780
Her body , yes . But not her dead body . That 's what I meant .

257
00:35:01,059 --> 00:35:05,206
Well , surely you don 't think she 's alive , in the hands of natives ?

258
00:35:05,230 --> 00:35:07,313
Oh no , better dead than that !

259
00:35:07,424 --> 00:35:09,947
Excuse me please , have you got a match ?

260
00:35:12,481 --> 00:35:13,544
Thank you .

261
00:35:20,399 --> 00:35:23,005
You don 't believe that , do you ?

262
00:35:24,273 --> 00:35:29,207
Say , there 's been lots of people that 's been pronounced dead

263
00:35:29,218 --> 00:35:31,703
that came alive again and lived for years .

264
00:35:31,727 --> 00:35:34,901
Now , if nature can play pranks like that ,

265
00:35:34,925 --> 00:35:37,842
why isn 't it possible to play pranks with nature ?

266
00:35:37,867 --> 00:35:39,210
Oh , I don 't know .

267
00:35:41,451 --> 00:35:47,213
Your driver believed he saw dead men , walking .

268
00:35:48,216 --> 00:35:52,518
He didn 't . What he saw was men alive

269
00:35:52,542 --> 00:35:54,713
and everything but this and this .

270
00:35:57,418 --> 00:36:00,779
Oh , the whole thing has me confused !

271
00:36:00,803 --> 00:36:02,494
I just can 't understand it .

272
00:36:02,721 --> 00:36:05,783
Um , I don 't blame you ... I don 't blame you .

273
00:36:05,807 --> 00:36:08,703
I 've been trying for years to get to the bottom of these things .

274
00:36:08,846 --> 00:36:11,971
To separate what you call fact from fiction .

275
00:36:12,493 --> 00:36:13,724
The law !

276
00:36:14,024 --> 00:36:18,226
The law of Haiti acknowledges the possibility of being buried alive .

277
00:36:18,427 --> 00:36:22,232
Here it is in the penal code . I 'll read it for you .

278
00:36:23,529 --> 00:36:25,082
It 's in French , do you speak French ?

279
00:36:25,106 --> 00:36:26,106
No .

280
00:36:27,088 --> 00:36:29,230
Excuse me please , have you got a match ?

281
00:36:29,369 --> 00:36:30,691
Right here , here 's one .

282
00:36:30,715 --> 00:36:32,215
Oh , thank you . I didn 't see it there .

283
00:36:32,364 --> 00:36:35,635
I 'll translate it for you . If you could spare me .

284
00:36:35,825 --> 00:36:37,037
Article ...

285
00:36:37,851 --> 00:36:39,637
Article 2.49 .

286
00:36:41,040 --> 00:36:45,394
The use ... The use of drugs or other practices

287
00:36:45,418 --> 00:36:50,675
which produce lethargic coma , or lifeless sleep ,

288
00:36:50,699 --> 00:36:54,444
shall be considered attempted murder .

289
00:36:55,207 --> 00:36:55,807
Attempted !

290
00:36:55,957 --> 00:36:56,968
Yes I see .

291
00:36:58,325 --> 00:37:01,328
If the person has been buried alive ,

292
00:37:01,352 --> 00:37:04,653
the act should be considered murder

293
00:37:04,677 --> 00:37:07,013
no matter what result follows .

294
00:37:08,269 --> 00:37:09,547
Beaumont !

295
00:37:10,446 --> 00:37:14,449
Say , you said you couldn 't understand why he was so interested in us .

296
00:37:14,812 --> 00:37:16,517
Do you think he did this ?

297
00:37:16,793 --> 00:37:19,052
No . No , I think his natives would .

298
00:37:19,102 --> 00:37:21,202
Natives would be right .

299
00:37:21,252 --> 00:37:24,253
Of course if you want to , we could go to Beaumont 's house first .

300
00:37:25,751 --> 00:37:31,302
If I could get my hands on the devil that 's responsible for this ,

301
00:37:31,326 --> 00:37:34,677
I 'll make him such an example that every witch doctor in Haiti

302
00:37:34,702 --> 00:37:36,470
would be shaking in his sandals .

303
00:37:36,494 --> 00:37:39,368
But we can 't do this alone .

304
00:37:39,392 --> 00:37:40,826
Can 't the authorities help ?

305
00:37:41,751 --> 00:37:46,464
The authorities , Neil , my boy , you don 't know these islands .

306
00:37:46,563 --> 00:37:49,214
The native authorities are afraid to meddle .

307
00:37:49,264 --> 00:37:52,566
I am not . I 've got friends among the natives .

308
00:37:52,918 --> 00:37:56,195
They 'll tell me things that no gendarme could ever get out of them .

309
00:37:57,119 --> 00:38:00,270
Because I am a preacher .

310
00:38:00,470 --> 00:38:01,993
They think I am a magician .

311
00:38:04,803 --> 00:38:09,673
Before we get through with this thing , we may uncover sins

312
00:38:09,698 --> 00:38:12,999
that even the devil would be ashamed of .

313
00:38:15,513 --> 00:38:18,680
Oh , these witch doctors ...

314
00:39:35,768 --> 00:39:36,813
Madeline ...

315
00:40:28,429 --> 00:40:34,333
Foolish things , they can 't bring back the light to those eyes .

316
00:40:37,663 --> 00:40:43,080
I was mad to do this , but if you had smiled on me ,

317
00:40:43,104 --> 00:40:47,138
I 'd have done anything for you , given you anything .

318
00:40:49,229 --> 00:40:56,594
I thought that beauty alone would satisfy , but the soul is gone ...

319
00:40:57,643 --> 00:41:01,344
I can 't bear those empty staring eyes .

320
00:41:04,528 --> 00:41:07,347
Oh , forgive me , Madeline . Forgive me !

321
00:41:09,212 --> 00:41:13,701
I can 't bear it any longer , I must take you back .

322
00:41:16,513 --> 00:41:19,953
Back to the grave , Monsieur ?

323
00:41:21,821 --> 00:41:28,256
No , you must put the life back into her eyes and bring laughter to her lips .

324
00:41:28,926 --> 00:41:31,259
She must be gay and happy again !

325
00:41:31,482 --> 00:41:34,705
You paint a charming picture , Monsieur .

326
00:41:34,976 --> 00:41:38,359
One that I should like to see myself !

327
00:42:00,461 --> 00:42:02,390
You must bring her back .

328
00:42:02,866 --> 00:42:06,250
Aren 't you a trifle afraid , Monsieur ?

329
00:42:06,603 --> 00:42:10,638
How do suppose those eyes will regard you

330
00:42:10,662 --> 00:42:13,313
when the brain is able to understand ?

331
00:42:46,537 --> 00:42:51,232
Better to see hatred in them than that dreadful emptiness .

332
00:42:51,560 --> 00:42:53,592
Perhaps you 're right .

333
00:42:54,091 --> 00:42:57,909
It would be a pity to destroy such a lovely flower .

334
00:43:00,351 --> 00:43:03,596
Let 's drink to the future of this flower .

335
00:43:03,620 --> 00:43:04,620
A glass of wine !

336
00:43:07,188 --> 00:43:11,755
Silver , bring wine ! We have a toast to drink .

337
00:43:39,839 --> 00:43:42,713
To the future , Monsieur !

338
00:43:58,147 --> 00:44:03,405
Only a pin point , Monsieur .

339
00:44:03,429 --> 00:44:04,635
In a flower ...

340
00:44:05,373 --> 00:44:09,123
or perhaps in a glass of wine ?

341
00:44:17,944 --> 00:44:20,448
You devil ! What are you trying to do to me ?

342
00:44:20,988 --> 00:44:24,616
I have other plans for Mademoiselle .

343
00:44:24,640 --> 00:44:28,163
And I am afraid you might not agree .

344
00:44:32,317 --> 00:44:37,142
I have taken a fancy to you , Monsieur !

345
00:44:37,980 --> 00:44:40,663
Silver ! Silver !

346
00:45:48,465 --> 00:45:49,965
Don 't , don 't !

347
00:46:20,908 --> 00:46:23,419
To the future , Monsieur !

348
00:46:49,713 --> 00:46:52,505
The vulture , you ...

349
00:47:01,796 --> 00:47:06,503
No . Not that . Not that !

350
00:47:12,333 --> 00:47:14,939
We ought to be picking up an old witch doctor around here pretty soon .

351
00:47:14,963 --> 00:47:19,051
His name is Pierre , I 've known him for years . Bright old fellow .

352
00:47:19,075 --> 00:47:22,846
I don 't know just where we 'll find him .

353
00:47:43,331 --> 00:47:49,441
Come , son . There are evil spirits in the road .

354
00:47:49,845 --> 00:47:57,845
I will give you an awonga . And here , this one for the ox .

355
00:48:08,690 --> 00:48:13,426
Young man is sick with distress .

356
00:48:13,685 --> 00:48:17,873
Well hey , wait a minute , we can 't afford to have you sick .

357
00:48:18,199 --> 00:48:22,068
Neil , why don 't you go over there , we 've got a hard day before us tomorrow .

358
00:48:24,532 --> 00:48:29,736
Now , now then Pierre , come on . He 's gone . We can talk .

359
00:48:29,761 --> 00:48:33,282
It is a dangerous thing you ask me to do .

360
00:48:33,307 --> 00:48:37,049
Well now listen here you know , we 're old friends , you and me ,

361
00:48:37,074 --> 00:48:38,690
and I want to go on .

362
00:48:38,714 --> 00:48:42,015
Turn back before it is too late !

363
00:48:42,538 --> 00:48:44,963
Oh , no . I 've come too far to turn back now .

364
00:48:45,251 --> 00:48:49,636
I 'm too old to go all this way with you .

365
00:48:49,791 --> 00:48:53,942
Well listen , can 't you get somebody to go with us ?

366
00:48:54,137 --> 00:48:58,444
My people all afraid of the mountain .

367
00:48:58,469 --> 00:48:59,554
Why ?

368
00:48:59,954 --> 00:49:06,548
Because it is called the land of the living dead .

369
00:49:06,752 --> 00:49:10,178
Well , have , have you ever been there ?

370
00:49:10,202 --> 00:49:17,738
I am the only man that has ever come back from there alive .

371
00:49:20,408 --> 00:49:28,058
There is an evil spirit man that is called Murder .

372
00:49:28,083 --> 00:49:34,459
Come , I will tell you all about what he did .

373
00:50:28,456 --> 00:50:29,457
Vulture .

374
00:50:40,583 --> 00:50:42,557
Just as old Pierre said .

375
00:50:43,861 --> 00:50:49,291
A cloud of vultures always hovers over the house of the living dead .

376
00:50:51,512 --> 00:50:52,516
Madeline ...

377
00:50:53,368 --> 00:50:54,905
Is she there ?

378
00:50:54,930 --> 00:50:57,169
Oh , I must go and see her .

379
00:50:57,194 --> 00:51:04,204
Neil , my boy , please , please lie down and rest . Please .

380
00:51:05,863 --> 00:51:08,110
You 'll feel stronger in the morning .

381
00:51:12,500 --> 00:51:13,500
You rest .

382
00:51:14,512 --> 00:51:17,237
Let me go up and see what I can do .

383
00:51:40,420 --> 00:51:42,723
Why is she so restless tonight ?

384
00:51:43,776 --> 00:51:46,456
Perhaps she remembers something ?

385
00:51:47,836 --> 00:51:52,651
They never remember anything when they are like that .

386
00:51:52,700 --> 00:51:53,732
No ?

387
00:51:54,515 --> 00:51:58,453
Because she 's cut off .

388
00:52:44,064 --> 00:52:45,064
Madeline !

389
00:52:46,597 --> 00:52:47,597
Madeline !

390
00:53:25,561 --> 00:53:27,425
No , no , I can 't ,

391
00:53:27,449 --> 00:53:28,538
I can 't !

392
00:53:28,562 --> 00:53:31,877
You must , it 's your turn .

393
00:53:31,901 --> 00:53:32,901
Let 's run away !

394
00:53:35,430 --> 00:53:37,489
He might hear you !

395
00:53:37,513 --> 00:53:41,801
No way . I can 't stand it . I am going to run away !

396
00:53:42,889 --> 00:53:46,303
He will find you and make you like her .

397
00:54:59,678 --> 00:55:01,530
Can you still hear me ?

398
00:55:08,559 --> 00:55:12,140
It is unfortunate you are no longer able to speak .

399
00:55:13,840 --> 00:55:17,336
I should be interested to hear you describe your symptoms ...

400
00:55:29,041 --> 00:55:35,444
You see , you are the first man to know what is happening .

401
00:55:40,188 --> 00:55:44,248
None of the others did .

402
00:56:05,274 --> 00:56:08,884
You refused to shake hands once .

403
00:56:09,778 --> 00:56:11,009
I remember .

404
00:56:12,840 --> 00:56:13,960
Well , well .

405
00:56:15,249 --> 00:56:17,711
We understand each other better now .

406
01:02:19,243 --> 01:02:20,664
Madeline !

407
01:02:26,511 --> 01:02:27,960
Madeline !

408
01:02:51,431 --> 01:02:52,727
Madeline !

409
01:02:55,645 --> 01:02:58,960
Madeline ! I found you !

410
01:02:58,984 --> 01:03:01,596
You 're alive . Alive !

411
01:03:02,527 --> 01:03:06,032
What 's the matter ? It 's I , Neil .

412
01:03:16,933 --> 01:03:21,339
Oh my darling , what have they done to you ?

413
01:03:41,297 --> 01:03:42,956
Who are you ?

414
01:03:45,452 --> 01:03:46,828
And what are they ?

415
01:03:46,992 --> 01:03:50,453
For you , my friend , they are the angels of death .

416
01:04:25,926 --> 01:04:29,401
Come ! Zombies ! Duck !

417
01:04:49,118 --> 01:04:50,275
Look !

418
01:05:38,427 --> 01:05:42,290
Madeline , don 't you know me , dear ?

419
01:05:42,604 --> 01:05:43,942
It 's Neil .

420
01:05:44,270 --> 01:05:48,800
I could swear , for a moment she recognized you .

421
01:05:51,533 --> 01:05:53,802
Come on , don 't let him get away !

422
01:06:51,404 --> 01:06:54,227
Madeline , my darling !

423
01:07:04,488 --> 01:07:08,710
Neil , I ... I dreamed ?

424
01:07:14,593 --> 01:07:19,958
Excuse me please , have you got a match ?

425
01:07:24,861 --> 01:07:29,630
